{
  "id": "80881",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Coefficients and Changes in Equilibrium",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Not all equilibrium problems are as straightforward as the ones seen in Module 4, Concepts of Chemical Equilibrium. For more complex problems, we must consider the relationships between the following:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "805279629",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The equilibrium constant expression "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2w2fnldgohvbe9j",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1679656225",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The coefficients in the balanced equation "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "r033p5y9drfsx4n",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3144878721",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "How changes in concentrations occur as a system reaches equilibrium  "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "w53dmrepdyioesy",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "939940954",
                "type": "li"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1629918580",
            "type": "ul"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Let's begin with the relationship between the coefficients of the balanced equation and what those coefficients indicate about how the concentrations of species (reactants and products) change as a reaction goes to completion. We know that the coefficients indicate the ratio of atoms and molecules that react and are produced in a reaction."
              }
            ],
            "id": "riz8mow0db073bz",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "For example, in the reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "tv0prk3aufqi2fb",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "h8v7xs66r5oc76w",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "v7a2h3ziy3rjdyx",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm O}_2(g)\\;\\rightarrow\\;2\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "we know that twice the number of moles of hydrogen molecules will react with oxygen molecules to produce the same number of moles of water molecules as the initial hydrogen molecules. "
              }
            ],
            "id": "9f46r7g69mw5sj6",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "If we have 1 mole of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and 1 mole of O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " in a reaction vessel and we add a spark to cause the reaction to occur, we will see the following changes in the amounts of reactants and products."
              }
            ],
            "id": "dzqa9yp744cwlrq",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "j3yk01j9vcbq98s",
                        "text": "Initial"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "h9undrk4bxw2nrv",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "65mkx56rsarsmjk",
                        "text": "1.0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "l3kp030poflojwp",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "lqc8h1ik3wnjckl",
                        "text": "1.0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "a8y6scpqiv0js0f",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "i4amewqj5otjjzs",
                        "text": "0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "509bf5ddc60nt6y",
                    "type": "td"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "l420psbvfws4izv",
                "type": "tr"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "ybamzsd6k4v64gt",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "Change"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "9xp53soc8ufkure",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "6t8e44cpak56mre",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "−1.0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "0nan0nzqbz3b5qy",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "jzzwz76v8mv04e0",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "−0.5 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "87r20ewr0qi306v",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "luvqjoyi8r6h7rw",
                        "strong": true,
                        "text": "+ 1.0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "w5p0220yq14ym5o",
                    "type": "td"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "rew96nhu4hmr1x4",
                "type": "tr"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "vlmrcp4x0oucxtq",
                        "text": "Final"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "6zptlvmdmen0j4g",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "9tq3t2eklbsotsh",
                        "text": "0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "jq7dzt9p0s30uv7",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "piesf0r5abl1sfu",
                        "text": "0.5 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "n0mpbsbdzdze7jc",
                    "type": "td"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "id": "6uih7lln8r25nh2",
                        "text": "+1.0 mol"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "qitdbmew8qkbuqa",
                    "type": "td"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "sgcce4vfl98ptn8",
                "type": "tr"
              }
            ],
            "id": "s4wwdx0k4s3fasr",
            "rowstyle": "alternating",
            "type": "table"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "change"
              },
              {
                "text": " that occurred from the initial amounts of reactants and product to the final amounts is based on the coefficients in the balanced equation. The same is true of reversible reactions as they reach equilibrium concentrations. For example, consider the following reversible reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "zg2ytqlzqslbsmd",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "meifzevpsbfz72p",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "200yka65rx63nnz",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The coefficients in this equation indicate that the same number of moles of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " will react to produce twice the number of moles of HI. So, given initial concentrations of reactants and products, H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " will decrease (or increase) by the same amount and the HI will increase (or decrease) by twice the amount of the H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "s2653tzm6f4n1zf",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "If the concentration of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " decreases by some value "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": ", the concentration of I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " will also decrease by that same value "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and the concentration of HI will increase by 2"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": ":"
              }
            ],
            "id": "2mckbry8gqf41b6",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "b8e7426uz7w1e7v",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "dobmgvf6dnbl6p3",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\begin{array}{l}{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)\\;\\\\-x\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;-x\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;+2x\\end{array}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Consider the following reversible reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "d9fgjs7tv1lmbh9",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "bdxxummov0ldekj",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "s0v719i5sea7x6w",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm{NH}}_3(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm N}_2(g)\\;+\\;3\\;{\\mathrm H}_2(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Let's assume for this reaction that the products, N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", decrease as the system reaches equilibrium. In that case, the concentration of NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " would increase. If N"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " decreases by some value "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": " as the system reaches equilibrium, H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " will decrease by 3"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": " and NH"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": " will increase by 2"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": ". "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}2\\;{\\mathrm{NH}}_3(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm N}_2(g)\\;+\\;3\\;{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\\\+2x\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;-x\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;-3x\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "9zego9c5r4oe3l8",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
